REGEX TIPS

Search and substitute patterns use Python regular expressions.
. matches any character; ^ and $ anchor a line; [] defines a character class.
*, +, ?, and {m,n} repeat; \d, \w, and \s match common character classes.
Groups use (...); replacements can reuse them with \1 or \g<1>.
Lowercase literal searches ignore case; uppercase or regex patterns are case-sensitive.
Substitute accepts any punctuation delimiter: :%s|/old/path|/new/path|g
A selected substitute delimiter cannot be backslash-escaped; choose another delimiter.
Substitute rejects CR/LF replacements; use :[range]! for multiline transforms.

